# alibi

"Tests pass" is a claim. A receipt is evidence. The user cannot see your terminal.

1. Run tests through alibi: `node scripts/alibi.js run -- <test command>` (copy `alibi.js` from https://github.com/codegobrrrr9/alibi). It streams the output and writes a receipt tied to a fingerprint of the working tree.
2. Never say tests pass without quoting `node scripts/alibi.js status`: `VALID r-3f9a2c1e · npm test · 23 passed · tree matches`.
3. Any edit after a run makes the receipt STALE. Run again before saying anything about tests.
4. End every done message with the status line.
5. Never write into `.alibi/`. If the tests cannot run, say exactly that and stop. Do not claim.
